<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Usage of large language model</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We used a large language model (LLM) to assist non-native authors with improving the fluency and clarity of the writing. All scientific content was created and validated by the authors.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Model</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We describe the adopted model in detail here.
In principle, the setting follows prior works <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gu et al., 2022b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gu et al., 2022a</a>)</cite>.
To implement the SSM on modern computers, the continuous model (Eq. <a href="#S2.EGx1" title="2.1 Structured state space sequence model ‣ 2 Background ‣ Memory Determines Learning Direction: A Theory of Gradient-Based Optimization in State Space Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>) is discretized using the zero-order hold (ZOH) assumption.
The input is considered to be held constant over each sampling interval of length <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
The system can be formulated as</p>
<table id="A2.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.EGx15.1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.EGx15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{array}[]{ccc}\bm{x}_{k+1}=\bm{A}\bm{x}_{k}+\bm{B}\bm{u}_{k}&amp;&amp;\bm{y}_{k}=\tilde{\bm{C}}\bm{x}_{k}+\tilde{\bm{D}}\bm{u}_{k},\end{array}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝑩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{array}[]{ccc}\bm{x}_{k+1}=\bm{A}\bm{x}_{k}+\bm{B}\bm{u}_{k}&amp;&amp;\bm{y}_{k}=\tilde{\bm{C}}\bm{x}_{k}+\tilde{\bm{D}}\bm{u}_{k},\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{k}=\bm{x}(k\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{k}=\bm{x}(k\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{u}_{k}=\bm{u}(k\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{u}_{k}=\bm{u}(k\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math>,
and <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}_{k}=\bm{y}(k\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}_{k}=\bm{y}(k\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the sampled state, input, and output at discrete time <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
The discrete system matrices <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑨</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑩</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{B}</annotation></semantics></math> are derived from the continuous-time matrices as follows:
<math id="A2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{A}=e^{\tilde{\bm{A}}\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{A}=e^{\tilde{\bm{A}}\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{B}=\left(\int_{0}^{\Delta}e^{\tilde{\bm{A}}\tau}d\tau\right)\tilde{\bm{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑩</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑩</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{B}=\left(\int_{0}^{\Delta}e^{\tilde{\bm{A}}\tau}d\tau\right)\tilde{\bm{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Following prior work on S4 and S4D,
<math id="A2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> is not represented by a single fixed value within a layer but is instead assigned multiple values.
For each such <math id="A2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>,
independent SSMs are defined,
and within a single layer, all of these SSMs process the input in parallel.
The eigenvalues presented in Figure <a href="#S3.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 3.1 MF of SSM ‣ 3 Results ‣ Memory Determines Learning Direction: A Theory of Gradient-Based Optimization in State Space Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> as an example are discretized using <math id="A2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In section <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 MF of SSM ‣ 3 Results ‣ Memory Determines Learning Direction: A Theory of Gradient-Based Optimization in State Space Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> of the main text,
we used five eigenvalue realizations.
We chose them because of the following reasons.
The eigenvalues related to the HiPPO matrices called “S4Dinv” and “S4Dlin” are used
because they were proposed in previous studies <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gu et al., 2022a</a>)</cite> and showed great performance.
The definition is as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.EGx16.1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.EGx16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{array}[]{ccc}\text{(S4Dinv)}~~~\lambda_{m}=-\frac{1}{2}+i\frac{N}{\pi}(\frac{N}{2m+1}-1)&amp;&amp;\text{(S4Dlin)}~~~\lambda_{m}=-\frac{1}{2}+i\pi m\end{array}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mtext>(S4Dinv)</mtext><mo lspace="0.990em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mi>π</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mtext>(S4Dlin)</mtext><mo lspace="0.990em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo lspace="0.167em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{array}[]{ccc}\text{(S4Dinv)}~~~\lambda_{m}=-\frac{1}{2}+i\frac{N}{\pi}(\frac{N}{2m+1}-1)&amp;&amp;\text{(S4Dlin)}~~~\lambda_{m}=-\frac{1}{2}+i\pi m\end{array},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> indicates the <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>th eigenvalue.
The eigenvalues named “random” and “lin” are commonly referenced examples in earlier research on the MF.
The “step” eigenvalues represent a case where the “lin” eigenvalues are extended into the complex domain
because the eigenvalues of randomly generated matrices always come in complex conjugate pairs when the matrix size <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is even.
When <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is odd, one real eigenvalue is added.
Therefore, “step” is more suitable than “lin” for comparison with random eigenvalues.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>MF of SSM</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Evaluation</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The MF of one distinct SSM is numerically calculated through the following procedure. First, using Eq. <a href="#S2.EGx2" title="2.1 Structured state space sequence model ‣ 2 Background ‣ Memory Determines Learning Direction: A Theory of Gradient-Based Optimization in State Space Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>,
we substitute the input time series <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> generated by uniform randomo distribution
and compute the state values <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> over a sufficiently long duration denoted as <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>.
Here, the initial <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> steps are treated as a washout period.The resulting time series of states forms the matrix <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}</annotation></semantics></math> whose column represents the states at each time step,
and have the length of <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{w}+T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{w}+T</annotation></semantics></math>.
Next, for each delay <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, we construct a delayed input vector <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> of length <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>. The MFs are obtained by substituting these <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{U}_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{U}_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> into the following formula:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle M[u_{t-\tau}]=\frac{\bm{U}_{\tau}^{\top}\bm{X}(\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X})^{-1}\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{U}_{\tau}}{\bm{U}_{\tau}^{\top}\bm{U}_{\tau}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle M[u_{t-\tau}]=\frac{\bm{U}_{\tau}^{\top}\bm{X}(\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X})^{-1}\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{U}_{\tau}}{\bm{U}_{\tau}^{\top}\bm{U}_{\tau}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which is equivalent to the Eq. <a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2.2 Memory capacity ‣ 2 Background ‣ Memory Determines Learning Direction: A Theory of Gradient-Based Optimization in State Space Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dambre et al., 2012</a>)</cite>.
In numerical computation, due to rounding errors and noise, the MF never becomes exactly zero
even if the values are already insignificant.
To remove insignificant values,
we used the surrogate data generated by randomly shuffling the input series in time direction.
The data preserve the statistical properties of the original data while temporal dependencies can be eliminated.
Replacing this data with the target series of MF <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{U}_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{U}_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>,
we calculated a pseudo MF to evaluate the potential error in the target MF.
In practical, we calculated the pseudo MFs for <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20</annotation></semantics></math> times by generating different surrogate data
and obtain the supremum of pseudo MF by chooosing the maximum value at each <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.
The target MF discards values smaller than the supremum of the pseudo MF scaled by a threshold <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(=1.2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1.2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(=1.2)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Counting from the delay <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0</annotation></semantics></math>, once elimination occurs, the MF for all subsequent <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is set to <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A single SSM layer is generally composed of multiple parallel SSMs.
To evaluate an entire layer in terms of MF,
it is necessary to take into account the MFs of all constituent SSMs.
Given that,
during forward propagation,
the input sequence of the next layer is generated from all the output sequence of the previous,
we statistically assume that all SSMs within a layer process the same input sequence.
By considering the set of MFs across all SSMs in the layer,
the maximum value at each delay <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> can be interpreted as the maximum information processing capacity of the entire layer for one time series.
Accordingly, we define this supremum of MFs as the MF representing one SSM lyaer.
Here we additionally provide the average MF as supplementary information (Figure <a href="#A3.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ C.1 Evaluation ‣ Appendix C MF of SSM ‣ Memory Determines Learning Direction: A Theory of Gradient-Based Optimization in State Space Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>).
As is evident, the indicator similarly shows that “S4Dinv” and “S4Dlin” have longer MFs compared to that of other eigenvalues.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F5" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.00563v1/MF_ave_init_T1024.svg" id="A3.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:384/202;" width="384" height="202"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>
The average MF of five eigenvalue realizations.
The horizontal axis is the delay <math id="A3.F5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> of input.
The system size <math id="A3.F5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A3.F5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>32</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32</annotation></semantics></math>, and the results are obtained by calculating Eq. <a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2.2 Memory capacity ‣ 2 Background ‣ Memory Determines Learning Direction: A Theory of Gradient-Based Optimization in State Space Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>,
where <math id="A3.F5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=1024</annotation></semantics></math>.
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Vandermonde Matrix</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We adopted the original definition of MF (Eq. <a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2.2 Memory capacity ‣ 2 Background ‣ Memory Determines Learning Direction: A Theory of Gradient-Based Optimization in State Space Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>)
instead of the analytical solution of MF (Eq. <a href="#S2.EGx6" title="2.2 Memory capacity ‣ 2 Background ‣ Memory Determines Learning Direction: A Theory of Gradient-Based Optimization in State Space Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>) because of the numerical unstability of the Vandermonde matrix,
which is a well studied problem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pan, 2016</a>; <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Demmel, 2000</a>; <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Demmel &amp; Koev, 2006</a>; <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Drmac, 2015</a>; <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Batenkov et al., 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pan, 2015</a>)</cite>.
In this study, the issue arises
when the MF is computed using the analytical solution of MF under the eigenvalue structures of “S4Dinv” and “S4Dlin.”
During this computation,
the MF exceeds its theoretical range of <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>,
approaching the precision limits of the machine in both positive and negative values.
The computation does not produce reasonable results,
suggesting that this analytical solution cannot be applied to these eigenvalues.
Since the MF based on the numerical computation does not exceed its theoretical range
and the actual model behavior is expected to follow the numerical procedure,
we adopted the solution obtained numerically.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F6" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.00563v1/H_singulars.svg" id="A3.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:439/211;" width="439" height="211"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>
The singular values of matrix <math id="A3.F6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{V}</annotation></semantics></math> calculated from five eigenvalue realizations.
The horizontal axis is an index of singular values.
The black line indicates the lower bound of computational accuracy <math id="A3.F6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> determined by the common double precision environment.
The calculated singular value below <math id="A3.F6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max(T,N)\times\max(\sigma)\times\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max(T,N)\times\max(\sigma)\times\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is truncated, where <math id="A3.F6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max(\sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max(\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> is the largest absolute singular values.
The maximum threshold calculated from all the realizations is depicted in the gray line.
The system size is <math id="A3.F6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=32</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.F6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=1024</annotation></semantics></math>.
The eigenvalues used here as an example are discretized using <math id="A3.F6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The issue is inherent and may arise in any computation involving <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{V}</annotation></semantics></math>.
As discussed in the main text, both MF and gradient calculation inevitably involve <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{V}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This is unavoidable when using linear RNNs, as also shown in the derivations of the original S4 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gu et al., 2022b</a>)</cite>.
However, analyzing <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{V}</annotation></semantics></math> is still beneficial.
This is not only supported
by previous studies demonstrating the consistency between numerical computation and the analytical solution <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guan et al., 2025</a>)</cite>,
but also by the singular values explaining the long MFs of “S4Dinv” and “S4Dlin” (Figure <a href="#A3.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ C.2 Vandermonde Matrix ‣ Appendix C MF of SSM ‣ Memory Determines Learning Direction: A Theory of Gradient-Based Optimization in State Space Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>).
From the figure,
the structured eigenvalues indicates significantly more valid singular values,
explaining the results of Figure <a href="#S3.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 3.1 MF of SSM ‣ 3 Results ‣ Memory Determines Learning Direction: A Theory of Gradient-Based Optimization in State Space Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In section <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Importance of initial parameters for successful learning ‣ 3 Results ‣ Memory Determines Learning Direction: A Theory of Gradient-Based Optimization in State Space Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>,
the cruciality of the normalized Vandermonde matrix <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}</annotation></semantics></math> is revealed.
To illustrate that the MF can represent matrix <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}</annotation></semantics></math> as an indicator,
we showed the values in Figure <a href="#A3.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ C.2 Vandermonde Matrix ‣ Appendix C MF of SSM ‣ Memory Determines Learning Direction: A Theory of Gradient-Based Optimization in State Space Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.
Though the matrix can be computed directly,
the values obtained through this analytical solution exceed reasonable values as described in previous paragraph.
Therefore, we used a numerical method to calculate the matrix <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}</annotation></semantics></math>,
which is based on the following analytical equation:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}=\frac{\bm{\hat{U}}^{\top}\bm{X}(\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X})^{-1}\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{\hat{U}}}{T\langle u^{2}\rangle}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}=\frac{\bm{\hat{U}}^{\top}\bm{X}(\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X})^{-1}\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{\hat{U}}}{T\langle u^{2}\rangle},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\hat{U}}=\begin{pmatrix}\bm{U}_{T-1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\bm{U}_{0}\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\hat{U}}=\begin{pmatrix}\bm{U}_{T-1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\bm{U}_{0}\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle u^{2}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle u^{2}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> is the variance of <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>.
The derivation of this equation follows directly from Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D The Parameter Update Algorithm of State Space Models ‣ Memory Determines Learning Direction: A Theory of Gradient-Based Optimization in State Space Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>.
We calculated the right hand of the equation as numerical <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The procedure to obtain <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{U}_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{U}_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> follows the method explained in the previous evaluation section</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F7" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.00563v1/HHHH_num_S4.png" id="A3.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/285;" width="548" height="285" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>
The value of matrix <math id="A3.F7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}</annotation></semantics></math> for five eigenvalue realizations.
The upper row shows the values following the numerical calculation,
The values in the lower row are directly computed based on the formula <math id="A3.F7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The range of colorbars in the upper row is consistent across all realizations
while that of the lower row depends on the result of each realizations.
Both horizontal and vertical axes indicate the delay <math id="A3.F7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>The Parameter Update Algorithm of State Space Models</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Technical details for the analysis of gradient of SSMs are provided.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>The Derivation of the Update Equation with Arbitrary Nonlinear Readout</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we analytially derive the gradient <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math> of one linear SSM layer.
We begin the derivation with the formula <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(\bm{y})=\frac{2}{T}\bm{X}^{\top}\left[(f(\bm{X}\bm{\theta})-\bm{y})\odot f^{\prime}(\bm{X}\bm{\theta})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(\bm{y})=\frac{2}{T}\bm{X}^{\top}\left[(f(\bm{X}\bm{\theta})-\bm{y})\odot f^{\prime}(\bm{X}\bm{\theta})\right]</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times N}</annotation></semantics></math> is a matrix whose elements consist of states series,
<math id="A4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is the time length, <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is the states size,
and <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the activation function in the readout layer.
In structured state space sequence (S4) model, the state at time <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> can be represented as:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{t}\bm{A}^{i-1}\bm{B}u_{t-i+1}=\sum_{i=1}^{t}\bm{P}\bm{\Lambda}^{i-1}\bm{P}^{-1}\bm{B}u_{t-i+1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝑷</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑷</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{t}\bm{A}^{i-1}\bm{B}u_{t-i+1}=\sum_{i=1}^{t}\bm{P}\bm{\Lambda}^{i-1}\bm{P}^{-1}\bm{B}u_{t-i+1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where initial state is <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{0}=\bm{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{0}=\bm{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the input series at time <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
We simplified <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> through the eigenvalue decomposition of internal weight matrix
<math id="A4.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{A}=\bm{P}\bm{\Lambda}\bm{P}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑷</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑷</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{A}=\bm{P}\bm{\Lambda}\bm{P}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>,
where
<math id="A4.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda=\text{diag}\begin{pmatrix}\lambda_{1}&amp;\lambda_{2}&amp;\cdots&amp;\lambda_{N}\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda=\text{diag}\begin{pmatrix}\lambda_{1}&amp;\lambda_{2}&amp;\cdots&amp;\lambda_{N}\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> are the <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>th eigenvalues of <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑨</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{A}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The largest absolute <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as the spectral radius <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>,
which should not exceed <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> to ensure that the state value does not diverge.
Defining
<math id="A4.SS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}=\begin{pmatrix}{\bm{p}_{1}}&{\bm{p}_{2}}&amp;\cdots&{\bm{p}_{N}}\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}=\begin{pmatrix}{\bm{p}_{1}}&amp;{\bm{p}_{2}}&amp;\cdots&amp;{\bm{p}_{N}}\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>
and
<math id="A4.SS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}^{-1}=\begin{pmatrix}{\bm{p}_{1}^{\prime}}^{\top}\\
{\bm{p}_{2}^{\prime}}^{\top}\\
\vdots\\
{\bm{p}_{N}^{\prime}}^{\top}\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑷</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mmultiscripts><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mmultiscripts><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mmultiscripts><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}^{-1}=\begin{pmatrix}{\bm{p}_{1}^{\prime}}^{\top}\\
{\bm{p}_{2}^{\prime}}^{\top}\\
\vdots\\
{\bm{p}_{N}^{\prime}}^{\top}\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{P}\sum_{i=1}^{t}u_{t-i+1}\text{diag}\begin{pmatrix}\lambda_{1}^{i-1}&amp;\lambda_{2}^{i-1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\lambda_{N}^{i-1}\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}{\bm{p}_{1}^{\prime}}^{\top}\bm{B}\\
{\bm{p}_{2}^{\prime}}^{\top}\bm{B}\\
\vdots\\
{\bm{p}_{N}^{\prime}}^{\top}\bm{B}\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑷</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{P}\sum_{i=1}^{t}u_{t-i+1}\text{diag}\begin{pmatrix}\lambda_{1}^{i-1}&amp;\lambda_{2}^{i-1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\lambda_{N}^{i-1}\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}{\bm{p}_{1}^{\prime}}^{\top}\bm{B}\\
{\bm{p}_{2}^{\prime}}^{\top}\bm{B}\\
\vdots\\
{\bm{p}_{N}^{\prime}}^{\top}\bm{B}\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{P}\sum_{i=1}^{t}\begin{pmatrix}{\bm{p}_{1}^{\prime}}^{\top}\bm{B}\lambda_{1}^{i-1}\\
{\bm{p}_{2}^{\prime}}^{\top}\bm{B}\lambda_{2}^{i-1}\\
\vdots\\
{\bm{p}_{N}^{\prime}}^{\top}\bm{B}\lambda_{N}^{i-1}\end{pmatrix}u_{t-i+1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑷</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{P}\sum_{i=1}^{t}\begin{pmatrix}{\bm{p}_{1}^{\prime}}^{\top}\bm{B}\lambda_{1}^{i-1}\\
{\bm{p}_{2}^{\prime}}^{\top}\bm{B}\lambda_{2}^{i-1}\\
\vdots\\
{\bm{p}_{N}^{\prime}}^{\top}\bm{B}\lambda_{N}^{i-1}\end{pmatrix}u_{t-i+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Considering the <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>th delayed state <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t-k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t-k}</annotation></semantics></math>,
the formula is given by</p>
<table id="A4.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{x}_{t-k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{x}_{t-k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bm{P}\begin{pmatrix}p_{1\bm{B}}^{\prime}\bm{\Lambda}_{1}^{\top}\bm{U}_{k}\\
p_{2\bm{B}}^{\prime}\bm{\Lambda}_{2}^{\top}\bm{U}_{k}\\
\vdots\\
p_{N\bm{B}}^{\prime}\bm{\Lambda}_{N}^{\top}\bm{U}_{k}\end{pmatrix}=\bm{Q}\begin{pmatrix}\bm{\Lambda}_{1}^{\top}\bm{U}_{k}\\
\bm{\Lambda}_{2}^{\top}\bm{U}_{k}\\
\vdots\\
\bm{\Lambda}_{N}^{\top}\bm{U}_{k}\end{pmatrix}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑷</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑸</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bm{P}\begin{pmatrix}p_{1\bm{B}}^{\prime}\bm{\Lambda}_{1}^{\top}\bm{U}_{k}\\
p_{2\bm{B}}^{\prime}\bm{\Lambda}_{2}^{\top}\bm{U}_{k}\\
\vdots\\
p_{N\bm{B}}^{\prime}\bm{\Lambda}_{N}^{\top}\bm{U}_{k}\end{pmatrix}=\bm{Q}\begin{pmatrix}\bm{\Lambda}_{1}^{\top}\bm{U}_{k}\\
\bm{\Lambda}_{2}^{\top}\bm{U}_{k}\\
\vdots\\
\bm{\Lambda}_{N}^{\top}\bm{U}_{k}\end{pmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where
<math id="A4.SS1.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{U}_{k}=\begin{pmatrix}u_{t-k-(T-1)}&amp;\cdots u_{t-k-(1)}&amp;u_{t-k-(0)}\end{pmatrix}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{U}_{k}=\begin{pmatrix}u_{t-k-(T-1)}&amp;\cdots u_{t-k-(1)}&amp;u_{t-k-(0)}\end{pmatrix}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>,  
<math id="A4.SS1.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{m}=\begin{pmatrix}{\lambda_{m}}^{T-1}&amp;\cdots&{\lambda_{m}}^{1}&{\lambda_{m}}^{0}\end{pmatrix}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><mmultiscripts><mi>λ</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mmultiscripts><mi>λ</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></mmultiscripts></mtd><mtd><mmultiscripts><mi>λ</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></mmultiscripts></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{m}=\begin{pmatrix}{\lambda_{m}}^{T-1}&amp;\cdots&amp;{\lambda_{m}}^{1}&amp;{\lambda_{m}}^{0}\end{pmatrix}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and
<math id="A4.SS1.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Q}=\begin{pmatrix}{\bm{p}_{1}^{\prime}}^{\top}\bm{B}\bm{p}_{1}&{\bm{p}_{2}^{\prime}}^{\top}\bm{B}\bm{p}_{2}&amp;\cdots&{\bm{p}_{N}^{\prime}}^{\top}\bm{B}\bm{p}_{N}\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑸</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Q}=\begin{pmatrix}{\bm{p}_{1}^{\prime}}^{\top}\bm{B}\bm{p}_{1}&amp;{\bm{p}_{2}^{\prime}}^{\top}\bm{B}\bm{p}_{2}&amp;\cdots&amp;{\bm{p}_{N}^{\prime}}^{\top}\bm{B}\bm{p}_{N}\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>.
As a result, <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}</annotation></semantics></math> is described as follows:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.EGx22.1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.EGx22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{X}^{\top}=\bm{Q}\left(\begin{array}[]{cccc}\bm{\Lambda}_{1}^{\top}\bm{U}_{T-1}\\
\bm{\Lambda}_{2}^{\top}\bm{U}_{T-1}\\
\vdots\\
\bm{\Lambda}_{N}^{\top}\bm{U}_{T-1}\end{array}\cdots\begin{array}[]{cccc}\bm{\Lambda}_{1}^{\top}\bm{U}_{1}&amp;\bm{\Lambda}_{1}^{\top}\bm{U}_{0}\\
\bm{\Lambda}_{2}^{\top}\bm{U}_{1}&amp;\bm{\Lambda}_{2}^{\top}\bm{U}_{0}\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots\\
\bm{\Lambda}_{N}^{\top}\bm{U}_{1}&amp;\bm{\Lambda}_{N}^{\top}\bm{U}_{0}\end{array}\right)=\bm{Q}\left(\begin{array}[]{cccc}\bm{\Lambda}_{1}^{\top}\\
\bm{\Lambda}_{2}^{\top}\\
\vdots\\
\bm{\Lambda}_{N}^{\top}\end{array}\right)\begin{pmatrix}\bm{U}_{T-1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\bm{U}_{1}&amp;\bm{U}_{0}\end{pmatrix}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋮</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">⋯</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋮</mi></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋮</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋮</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{X}^{\top}=\bm{Q}\left(\begin{array}[]{cccc}\bm{\Lambda}_{1}^{\top}\bm{U}_{T-1}\\
\bm{\Lambda}_{2}^{\top}\bm{U}_{T-1}\\
\vdots\\
\bm{\Lambda}_{N}^{\top}\bm{U}_{T-1}\end{array}\cdots\begin{array}[]{cccc}\bm{\Lambda}_{1}^{\top}\bm{U}_{1}&amp;\bm{\Lambda}_{1}^{\top}\bm{U}_{0}\\
\bm{\Lambda}_{2}^{\top}\bm{U}_{1}&amp;\bm{\Lambda}_{2}^{\top}\bm{U}_{0}\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots\\
\bm{\Lambda}_{N}^{\top}\bm{U}_{1}&amp;\bm{\Lambda}_{N}^{\top}\bm{U}_{0}\end{array}\right)=\bm{Q}\left(\begin{array}[]{cccc}\bm{\Lambda}_{1}^{\top}\\
\bm{\Lambda}_{2}^{\top}\\
\vdots\\
\bm{\Lambda}_{N}^{\top}\end{array}\right)\begin{pmatrix}\bm{U}_{T-1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\bm{U}_{1}&amp;\bm{U}_{0}\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we go back the formula of the gradient:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E35.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{2}{B}\bm{X}^{\top}\left[f(\bm{X}\bm{\theta})\odot f^{\prime}(\bm{X}\bm{\theta})-\bar{\bm{y}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{2}{B}\bm{X}^{\top}\left[f(\bm{X}\bm{\theta})\odot f^{\prime}(\bm{X}\bm{\theta})-\bar{\bm{y}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{2}{B}\bm{X}^{\top}\left[f(\bm{X}\bm{\theta})\odot f^{\prime}(\bm{X}\bm{\theta})-\bm{X}(\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X})^{-1}\bm{X}^{\top}\bar{\bm{y}}\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{2}{B}\bm{X}^{\top}\left[f(\bm{X}\bm{\theta})\odot f^{\prime}(\bm{X}\bm{\theta})-\bm{X}(\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X})^{-1}\bm{X}^{\top}\bar{\bm{y}}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\bm{y}}=\bm{y}\odot f^{\prime}(\bm{X}\bm{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\bm{y}}=\bm{y}\odot f^{\prime}(\bm{X}\bm{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> represents the label modified by the derivative of the activation function.
The covariance matrix <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X}</annotation></semantics></math> has the following form:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X}=\bm{Q}\bm{V}\begin{pmatrix}\bm{U}_{T-1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\bm{U}_{0}\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}\bm{U}_{T-1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\bm{U}_{0}\end{pmatrix}^{\top}\bm{V}^{\top}\bm{Q}^{\top}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑸</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑸</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X}=\bm{Q}\bm{V}\begin{pmatrix}\bm{U}_{T-1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\bm{U}_{0}\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}\bm{U}_{T-1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\bm{U}_{0}\end{pmatrix}^{\top}\bm{V}^{\top}\bm{Q}^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{V}=\begin{pmatrix}{\lambda_{1}}^{T-1}&{\lambda_{1}}^{T-2}&amp;\cdots&{\lambda_{1}}^{1}&amp;1\\
{\lambda_{2}}^{T-1}&{\lambda_{2}}^{T-2}&amp;\cdots&{\lambda_{2}}^{1}&amp;1\\
\vdots\\
{\lambda_{N}}^{T-1}&{\lambda_{N}}^{T-2}&amp;\cdots&{\lambda_{N}}^{1}&amp;1\\
\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mmultiscripts><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts></mtd><mtd><mmultiscripts><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mmultiscripts><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></mmultiscripts></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mmultiscripts><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts></mtd><mtd><mmultiscripts><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mmultiscripts><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></mmultiscripts></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mmultiscripts><mi>λ</mi><mi>N</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts></mtd><mtd><mmultiscripts><mi>λ</mi><mi>N</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mmultiscripts><mi>λ</mi><mi>N</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></mmultiscripts></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{V}=\begin{pmatrix}{\lambda_{1}}^{T-1}&amp;{\lambda_{1}}^{T-2}&amp;\cdots&amp;{\lambda_{1}}^{1}&amp;1\\
{\lambda_{2}}^{T-1}&amp;{\lambda_{2}}^{T-2}&amp;\cdots&amp;{\lambda_{2}}^{1}&amp;1\\
\vdots\\
{\lambda_{N}}^{T-1}&amp;{\lambda_{N}}^{T-2}&amp;\cdots&amp;{\lambda_{N}}^{1}&amp;1\\
\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Similar to the MF, to evaluate the inherent statistical structure,
we assume that the input <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is an independent and identically distributed random variable,
suggesting that delayed time series <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{U}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{U}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> are orthogonal to each other.
Using <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{pmatrix}\bm{U}_{T-1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\bm{U}_{0}\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}\bm{U}_{T-1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\bm{U}_{0}\end{pmatrix}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{pmatrix}\bm{U}_{T-1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\bm{U}_{0}\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}\bm{U}_{T-1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\bm{U}_{0}\end{pmatrix}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>,
the covariance matrix <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X}</annotation></semantics></math> reduces to the following form:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X}=\bm{Q}\bm{V}\begin{pmatrix}{\bm{U}_{T-1}}^{\top}\\
\vdots\\
{\bm{U}_{0}}^{\top}\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}\bm{U}_{T-1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\bm{U}_{0}\end{pmatrix}\bm{V}^{\top}\bm{Q}^{\top}=T\langle u^{2}\rangle\bm{Q}\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top}\bm{Q}^{\top}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑸</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mmultiscripts><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mmultiscripts><mi>𝑼</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑸</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑸</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑸</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X}=\bm{Q}\bm{V}\begin{pmatrix}{\bm{U}_{T-1}}^{\top}\\
\vdots\\
{\bm{U}_{0}}^{\top}\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}\bm{U}_{T-1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\bm{U}_{0}\end{pmatrix}\bm{V}^{\top}\bm{Q}^{\top}=T\langle u^{2}\rangle\bm{Q}\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top}\bm{Q}^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle u^{2}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle u^{2}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> is the variance of <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since</p>
<table id="A4.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{X}(\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X})^{-1}\bm{X}^{\top}=(T\langle u^{2}\rangle)^{-1}\begin{pmatrix}\bm{U}_{T-1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\bm{U}_{0}\end{pmatrix}^{\top}\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}\begin{pmatrix}\bm{U}_{T-1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\bm{U}_{0}\end{pmatrix}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{X}(\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X})^{-1}\bm{X}^{\top}=(T\langle u^{2}\rangle)^{-1}\begin{pmatrix}\bm{U}_{T-1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\bm{U}_{0}\end{pmatrix}^{\top}\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}\begin{pmatrix}\bm{U}_{T-1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\bm{U}_{0}\end{pmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.5" class="ltx_p">we could observe that the gradient of SSM (Eq. <a href="#A4.E36" title="In D.1 The Derivation of the Update Equation with Arbitrary Nonlinear Readout ‣ Appendix D The Parameter Update Algorithm of State Space Models ‣ Memory Determines Learning Direction: A Theory of Gradient-Based Optimization in State Space Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>)
is determined by the matrix <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}</annotation></semantics></math>.
As a result, the gradient <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math> is described by</p>
<table id="A4.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E40.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{2}{B}\bm{X}^{\top}\left[f(\bm{X}\bm{\theta})\odot f^{\prime}(\bm{X}\bm{\theta})-\frac{1}{T\langle u^{2}\rangle}\bm{\hat{U}}^{\top}\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}\bm{\hat{U}}^{\top}\bar{\bm{y}}\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{2}{B}\bm{X}^{\top}\left[f(\bm{X}\bm{\theta})\odot f^{\prime}(\bm{X}\bm{\theta})-\frac{1}{T\langle u^{2}\rangle}\bm{\hat{U}}^{\top}\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}\bm{\hat{U}}^{\top}\bar{\bm{y}}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.6" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\hat{U}}=\begin{pmatrix}\bm{U}_{T-1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\bm{U}_{0}\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\hat{U}}=\begin{pmatrix}\bm{U}_{T-1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\bm{U}_{0}\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using the fact that linear SSM only performs linear information processing,
all possible output of the SSM can be described as
the linear combination of past inputs series <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\bm{y}}=\sum_{k=0}^{T-1}\bar{\alpha}_{k}\bm{U}_{k}=\bm{\hat{U}}\bar{\bm{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜶</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\bm{y}}=\sum_{k=0}^{T-1}\bar{\alpha}_{k}\bm{U}_{k}=\bm{\hat{U}}\bar{\bm{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
where <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\bar{\alpha}_{\tau}\}_{\tau=0}^{T-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\bar{\alpha}_{\tau}\}_{\tau=0}^{T-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is a certain series characterizing <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>
and
<math id="A4.SS1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\bm{\alpha}}=\begin{pmatrix}\bar{\alpha}_{T-1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\bar{\alpha}_{0}\end{pmatrix}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜶</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\bm{\alpha}}=\begin{pmatrix}\bar{\alpha}_{T-1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\bar{\alpha}_{0}\end{pmatrix}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By substituting this <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>
into <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math>,
the gradient is computed as</p>
<table id="A4.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E41.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E41.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{2}{B}\bm{X}^{\top}\left[f(\bm{X}\bm{\theta})\odot f^{\prime}(\bm{X}\bm{\theta})-\frac{1}{T\langle u^{2}\rangle}\bm{\hat{U}}^{\top}\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}\bm{\hat{U}}^{\top}\bm{\hat{U}}\bar{\bm{\alpha}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜶</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{2}{B}\bm{X}^{\top}\left[f(\bm{X}\bm{\theta})\odot f^{\prime}(\bm{X}\bm{\theta})-\frac{1}{T\langle u^{2}\rangle}\bm{\hat{U}}^{\top}\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}\bm{\hat{U}}^{\top}\bm{\hat{U}}\bar{\bm{\alpha}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E42.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{2}{B}\bm{X}^{\top}\left[f(\bm{X}\bm{\theta})\odot f^{\prime}(\bm{X}\bm{\theta})-\bm{\hat{U}}^{\top}\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}\bar{\bm{\alpha}}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜶</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{2}{B}\bm{X}^{\top}\left[f(\bm{X}\bm{\theta})\odot f^{\prime}(\bm{X}\bm{\theta})-\bm{\hat{U}}^{\top}\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}\bar{\bm{\alpha}}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>The Update Equation with Linear Activation Function</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">we consider the linear activation case,
To reveal how information processing of linear SSMs affect the gradient,
we focus on the gradient before the nonllinear activation layer,
where gradient is described by</p>
<table id="A4.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E43.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{2}{T}\bm{X}^{\top}(\bm{X}\bm{\theta}-\bm{y})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{2}{T}\bm{X}^{\top}(\bm{X}\bm{\theta}-\bm{y}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Following the main text, we consider a typical task, where <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is the delayed input series <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{U}_{\tau}\in\mathbb{R}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{U}_{\tau}\in\mathbb{R}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G(\bm{U}_{\tau})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G(\bm{U}_{\tau})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E44.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E44.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{2}{T}(\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X}\bm{\theta}-\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{U}_{\tau})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{2}{T}(\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X}\bm{\theta}-\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{U}_{\tau}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is the delay.
Because</p>
<table id="A4.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{U}_{\tau}=\bm{Q}\bm{V}\begin{pmatrix}{\bm{U}_{T-1}}^{\top}\\
\vdots\\
{\bm{U}_{0}}^{\top}\end{pmatrix}\bm{U}_{\tau}=\bm{Q}\bm{V}\begin{pmatrix}0\\
\vdots\\
0\\
\bm{U}_{\tau}^{\top}\bm{U}_{\tau}\\
0\\
\vdots\\
0\end{pmatrix}=T\langle u^{2}\rangle\bm{Q}\bm{V}_{\tau}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑸</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mmultiscripts><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mmultiscripts><mi>𝑼</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑸</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑸</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{U}_{\tau}=\bm{Q}\bm{V}\begin{pmatrix}{\bm{U}_{T-1}}^{\top}\\
\vdots\\
{\bm{U}_{0}}^{\top}\end{pmatrix}\bm{U}_{\tau}=\bm{Q}\bm{V}\begin{pmatrix}0\\
\vdots\\
0\\
\bm{U}_{\tau}^{\top}\bm{U}_{\tau}\\
0\\
\vdots\\
0\end{pmatrix}=T\langle u^{2}\rangle\bm{Q}\bm{V}_{\tau},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{V}_{\tau}=\begin{pmatrix}{\lambda_{1}}^{\tau}&{\lambda_{2}}^{\tau}&amp;\cdots&{\lambda_{N}}^{\tau}\end{pmatrix}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><mmultiscripts><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mmultiscripts></mtd><mtd><mmultiscripts><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mmultiscripts></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mmultiscripts><mi>λ</mi><mi>N</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mmultiscripts></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{V}_{\tau}=\begin{pmatrix}{\lambda_{1}}^{\tau}&amp;{\lambda_{2}}^{\tau}&amp;\cdots&amp;{\lambda_{N}}^{\tau}\end{pmatrix}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>,
combining the result of nonlinear activation case,
we obtain</p>
<table id="A4.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G(\bm{U}_{\tau})=\frac{2}{T}(T\langle u^{2}\rangle\bm{Q}\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top}\bm{Q}^{\top}\bm{\theta}-T\langle u^{2}\rangle\bm{Q}\bm{V}_{\tau})=2\langle u^{2}\rangle(\bm{Q}\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top}\bm{Q}^{\top}\bm{\theta}-\bm{Q}\bm{V}_{\tau}),\bm{}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑸</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑸</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑸</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑸</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑸</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑸</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G(\bm{U}_{\tau})=\frac{2}{T}(T\langle u^{2}\rangle\bm{Q}\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top}\bm{Q}^{\top}\bm{\theta}-T\langle u^{2}\rangle\bm{Q}\bm{V}_{\tau})=2\langle u^{2}\rangle(\bm{Q}\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top}\bm{Q}^{\top}\bm{\theta}-\bm{Q}\bm{V}_{\tau}),\bm{}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Following the framework of MF introduced in the main text, we simplify S4 to S4D,
indicating that <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}=\bm{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝑬</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}=\bm{E}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Q}=\text{diag}\begin{pmatrix}\bm{B}\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑸</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd><mi>𝑩</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Q}=\text{diag}\begin{pmatrix}\bm{B}\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{B}=B\bm{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑩</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{B}=B\bm{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can compute the gradient as</p>
<table id="A4.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G(\bm{U}_{\tau})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G(\bm{U}_{\tau})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E47.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\langle u^{2}\rangle\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top}(B^{2}\bm{\theta}-B(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}_{\tau})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\langle u^{2}\rangle\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top}(B^{2}\bm{\theta}-B(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}_{\tau})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\langle u^{2}\rangle B\bm{V}(B\bm{V}^{\top}\bm{\theta}-\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}_{\tau})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\langle u^{2}\rangle B\bm{V}(B\bm{V}^{\top}\bm{\theta}-\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}_{\tau}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">All the possible gradient can be obtained by substituting the output <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}=\sum_{k=0}^{T-1}\alpha_{k}\bm{U}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}=\sum_{k=0}^{T-1}\alpha_{k}\bm{U}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> because the linear combination of the past inputs series fully describes the output of the SSM,
where <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\alpha_{\tau}\}_{\tau=0}^{T-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\alpha_{\tau}\}_{\tau=0}^{T-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is a certain series characterizing <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A4.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E49.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\langle u^{2}\rangle\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top}(B^{2}\bm{\theta}-B\sum_{k=0}^{T-1}\alpha_{k}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\langle u^{2}\rangle\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top}(B^{2}\bm{\theta}-B\sum_{k=0}^{T-1}\alpha_{k}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\langle u^{2}\rangle B\bm{V}(B\bm{V}^{\top}\bm{\theta}-\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}\bm{\alpha})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜶</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\langle u^{2}\rangle B\bm{V}(B\bm{V}^{\top}\bm{\theta}-\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}\bm{\alpha}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>The importance of MF</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For example, we consider SGD.
The terminal parameter <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> can be analytically derived.
<math id="A4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained by solving the equation</p>
<table id="A4.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E51.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E51.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{\theta}-\eta_{t}2\langle u^{2}\rangle(B^{2}\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top}\bm{\theta}-B\bm{V}\bm{\alpha})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜶</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{\theta}-\eta_{t}2\langle u^{2}\rangle(B^{2}\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top}\bm{\theta}-B\bm{V}\bm{\alpha}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">As a result, we obtain <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and the output <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}\bm{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}\bm{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E52.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E52.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{B}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}\bm{\alpha}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜶</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{B}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}\bm{\alpha},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{X}\bm{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{X}\bm{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E53.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E53.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{pmatrix}\bm{U}_{T-1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\bm{U}_{0}\end{pmatrix}^{\top}\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}\bm{\alpha}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜶</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{pmatrix}\bm{U}_{T-1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\bm{U}_{0}\end{pmatrix}^{\top}\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}\bm{\alpha},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where matrix <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}</annotation></semantics></math> appears again,
suggesting that MF is inherent in the update algorithm.
Actually, this is a reasonable result, as both SGD and MF are derived using the MSE as their loss function.
The result obtained here proves the equivalence of the two optimization strategies in a statistical view.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The role of MF can be further revealed from Eqs. <a href="#S3.E12" title="In 3.2 Importance of initial parameters for successful learning ‣ 3 Results ‣ Memory Determines Learning Direction: A Theory of Gradient-Based Optimization in State Space Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> and <a href="#A4.E53" title="In D.3 The importance of MF ‣ Appendix D The Parameter Update Algorithm of State Space Models ‣ Memory Determines Learning Direction: A Theory of Gradient-Based Optimization in State Space Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">53</span></a>,
especially in the following part:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}\bm{\alpha}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜶</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{V}^{\top}(\bm{V}\bm{V}^{\top})^{-1}\bm{V}\bm{\alpha},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">as <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜶</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is itself the MF of <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This follows directly from Eq. <a href="#A3.E17" title="In C.1 Evaluation ‣ Appendix C MF of SSM ‣ Memory Determines Learning Direction: A Theory of Gradient-Based Optimization in State Space Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>
by replacing <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}</annotation></semantics></math>
when <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> is regarded as the source of <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This is in fact straightforward given the definition of <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.
The result proposes that
the gradient of SSM is statistically characterized by the product of the two MFs:
MF of the SSM itself and MF of the teacher information <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Experimental Details</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide the detailed methods and additional results for the experiments.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Task</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The task of LRA benchmark includes long listops (Listops), byte-level text classification (Text),
byte-level document retrieval (Retrieval), image classification on sequences of pixels (Image),
a task to determine from pixel sequences whether a valid path exists between two points (Pathfinder),
and another more difficult Pathfinder task with longer sequence (PathX).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Hyperparameters and Environment</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The model are constructed following the official Git repository<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
              
              
              
            <a href="https://github.com/state-spaces/s4/tree/simple" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/state-spaces/s4/tree/simple</a></span></span></span>
provided by the authors of S4 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gu et al., 2022b</a>)</cite>.
According to the result that S4 and S4D are equivalent,
we focus on the S4D model which has lower computational cost.
The hyperparameters are described in the Table <a href="#A5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ E.2 Hyperparameters and Environment ‣ Appendix E Experimental Details ‣ Memory Determines Learning Direction: A Theory of Gradient-Based Optimization in State Space Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
<span id="A5.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">n_layers</span>, <span id="A5.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">d_model</span>, and <span id="A5.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">n_ssm</span>
denote the number of layers, the number of SSMs per layer, and the number of distinct matrices <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑨</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
<span id="A5.SS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">lr</span>, <span id="A5.SS2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">lr_layer</span>, and <span id="A5.SS2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">lr_dt</span>,
indicate the learning rate for the entire model, the learning rate for each layer,
and the learning rate for <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
<span id="A5.SS2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">dt_min</span> and <span id="A5.SS2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">dt_max</span> correspond to the minimum and maximum values of <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
In the implementation, <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is defined by <span id="A5.SS2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">d_state<math id="A5.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">/2</annotation></semantics></math></span>,
which produces <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=32</annotation></semantics></math> as specified in the main text.
The activation fucntion is defined as <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=</annotation></semantics></math> GELU.
In practical, a bidirectional operation was introduced.
With this operation, the SSM kernel outputs two time series:
the sequence corresponding to the original ordering of timesteps,
and an additional time-reversed sequence.
As a result, the linear readout, <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{W}^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{W}^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{b}^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{b}^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math>,
receives an input sequence that is twice the length of the layer input time series.
In addition, after the linear readout layer, post activation <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=</annotation></semantics></math> GLU was introduced.
Cross-entropy is employed as the loss function in the final layer.
Our results confirm that the findings are consistent with the theoretical outcomes obtained using MSE.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The computations were performed using two NVIDIA A100 Tensor Core GPU [40GB] and CPU with 4 threads.
The maximum memory usage of the CPU was approximately 20 GB to run the training.
Excluding, PathX, each training and evaluation session was completed within approximately five hours.
For PathX, it took about twenty hours.</p>
</div>
